   $q$What does the last stanza suggest about the two meets?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker enjoyed the first meet more than the last one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The setting stayed the same, so the better result came from the swimmer's growth.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The crowd was louder in August, which helped the speaker swim faster.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The August meet was easier because the pool was smaller.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The setting stayed the same, so the better result came from the swimmer's growth.$q$, $q$The stanza repeats that the pool, water and crowd were all the same, then says, "The swimmer was the one who changed." The crowd "cheered just as loud," so it was not louder in August.$q$, 'draft', '3fc3dd75-bda6-507e-bc78-993282894856')
