insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('749c0c19-26f4-5385-abf9-976f9efabd9b', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Caught by the Weather$q$, $q$Text 1: Fog on Ridge Trail (an adventure story)

Diego and his aunt Lupe were halfway up Ridge Trail when a thick fog rolled in. Soon Diego could not see the next trail marker. His heart pounded. "Let's run back down!" he said.

"Not yet," said Aunt Lupe. "First we stop and think." She pulled a paper map and a compass from her pack. Before the hike, she had marked their route in pencil.

Together they found the stream on the map. They could hear it splashing to their left. "The trail follows the stream down," Aunt Lupe said. Step by step, they walked beside the water. An hour later, they reached the parking lot, damp but safe.

Text 2: The Island Crossing (an adventure story)

Amara and her friend Tavi paddled their canoe toward Gull Island. The water was calm and the sky was bright. They had forgotten to check the weather report, but it did not seem to matter.

Halfway across, the wind picked up. Waves slapped the canoe. Tavi wanted to paddle hard for the island, but it was still far away. Amara looked back. The shore they had left was much closer.

"We turn around," she said. "The island will still be there tomorrow." They paddled back slowly, keeping the canoe pointed into the waves. On the beach, Amara wrote a note in her journal: Check the weather first.$q$, 'draft')
