-- Passage rg5-comparing-texts-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('27a8833b-f948-53b3-b306-aae747129353', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Far from Earth$q$, $q$Text 1: Rain in Dome Seven (science fiction)

Zuri had lived in Dome Seven on Mars for three years. The dome had lights, gardens and even a swimming pool. But Zuri missed rain.

She asked the engineer, Mr. Petrov, if she could borrow the garden sprinklers for one hour. She set them to spray high into the air and dimmed the lights to gray. Then she invited the other kids.

They stood under the falling drops with their faces turned up. Little Omar had been born on Mars, and he had never felt rain. He giggled and stuck out his tongue. "Is this what Earth is like?" he asked.

"Sometimes," Zuri said, smiling.

Text 2: The Window (science fiction)

Aboard the space station Horizon, Mateo had a job. Each morning he checked the plant trays. It was a good job, but he felt homesick. He missed the smell of his grandmother's kitchen and the sound of dogs barking on his street.

One night, he could not sleep. He floated to the big round window. Below him, Earth turned slowly, blue and white and shining. Mateo found the coast where his town was. A tiny cluster of lights glowed there.

"Goodnight, Abuela," he whispered. He did not feel quite so far away anymore. After that, Mateo visited the window every night before bed.$q$, 'draft')
