   $q$How do signals along one road work together to create a green wave?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each light stays green until the sensor sees that no more cars are left on the road.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-events"},{"text":"Drivers who speed up can reach every light before it has a chance to turn red.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"All the lights on the road turn green at exactly the same moment for every driver.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Each light turns green a few seconds after the one before it, matching steady traffic.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each light turns green a few seconds after the one before it, matching steady traffic.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 says the next light turns green a few seconds after the one before, so cars moving at the speed limit pass several greens in a row. The wave works for cars at the speed limit, not for drivers who speed up.$q$, 'draft', 'dc9c3009-8bec-5c9a-a029-624619b4617c')
