insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('73963a3e-e034-51c3-a4b6-c95f5a26cdee', 'rg5-context-clues-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Kite Festival$q$, $q$Every spring, the town of Willow Bend holds a kite festival on the hill behind the library. This year, Ama and her little brother Kofi built a kite shaped like a dragon.

On the morning of the festival, the weather was ideal for flying. A steady breeze blew, and there was not a single cloud. Ama could hardly wait.

The hill was crowded with families. Kites of every color filled the sky. Some were plain diamonds, but others were elaborate, with long ribbon tails, painted scales, and many moving parts.

Ama and Kofi ran down the slope, and their dragon rose into the air. Then the wind suddenly gusted. The kite dipped and spun in circles. Kofi gripped the string tightly so it would not escape his hands.

At last the wind calmed, and the dragon soared high above the trees. A judge walked by and stopped. She was impressed, and she wrote their names on her clipboard. That afternoon, the dragon kite won the prize for best design.$q$, 'draft')
