   $q$In paragraph 3, the "nozzle" squeezes out plastic. Which comparison helps explain what a nozzle is?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It works like a computer screen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"It works like a strand of plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-details"},{"text":"It works like a sheet of flat paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"It works like the tip of a frosting bag.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It works like the tip of a frosting bag.$q$, $q$The text compares the nozzle to "frosting coming out of a decorating bag," showing that a nozzle is a narrow opening that pushes something out. The strand of plastic is what goes into the nozzle, not the nozzle itself.$q$, 'draft', 'c240ec2e-cb02-59c4-bc33-a2a5fa086273')
