   $q$In paragraph 1, the coach tells Hana not to "sprint" at the beginning. What does "sprint" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"run as fast as you can for a short time","is_correct":true},{"text":"walk slowly and rest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"climb up a steep hill","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"stretch before a race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$run as fast as you can for a short time$q$, $q$The coach says to "save your energy," and at the start "many runners dashed ahead," so sprinting means running very fast and using up energy. The hill comes later and is a separate part of the race.$q$, 'draft', '01d5406e-1c96-59ca-8493-66507ea82909')
