   $q$According to the passage, why does a hummingbird gain weight before it migrates?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The extra weight helps it scare other birds away from feeders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The extra fat keeps it warm while it rests in cold places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The extra weight keeps the strong sea winds from blowing it away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The extra fat gives it energy to burn during the long flight.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The extra fat gives it energy to burn during the long flight.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says the fat is something "the bird burns like fuel during the long flight." The passage never mentions wind or warmth as reasons for gaining weight.$q$, 'draft', '31eed681-81aa-5f68-b72d-83a9486dcc88')
