   $q$Which quotation shows that hummingbirds do not migrate in groups?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Hummingbirds travel alone, not in flocks.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"To get ready, a hummingbird eats and eats.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"People can help hummingbirds along the way.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"Some cross a wide stretch of sea without stopping.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Hummingbirds travel alone, not in flocks."$q$, $q$The sentence "Hummingbirds travel alone, not in flocks" says directly that they do not fly in groups. Crossing the sea without stopping tells about the route, not whether the birds travel together.$q$, 'draft', '31eed681-81aa-5f68-b72d-83a9486dcc88')
