   $q$A student says, "The towers hold up the whole bridge all by themselves." Which quotation best shows that this statement is not accurate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Then they string two main cables over the tops of the towers.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"\"The suspenders pass that pull to the main cables, and the main cables pass it to the towers and anchorages.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"The road seems to float in the air.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"First, builders put up two tall towers, one near each shore.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-wrong-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"The suspenders pass that pull to the main cables, and the main cables pass it to the towers and anchorages."$q$, $q$This sentence shows the load goes to the towers "and anchorages," so the towers share the work. The sentence about stringing cables over the towers mentions towers but does not show where the weight goes.$q$, 'draft', '290c9b49-2cf4-5706-8df6-56df663afd45')
