   $q$Which quotation best supports the idea that sport wheelchairs are designed with safety in mind?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Today, teams play in schools, colleges and community leagues.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"A small extra wheel sticks out the back to keep the chair from flipping backward.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"A sport wheelchair looks different from an everyday one.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"\"Players shoot, pass and dribble, just like in any other game.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"A small extra wheel sticks out the back to keep the chair from flipping backward."$q$, $q$The extra wheel exists to stop the chair from "flipping backward," which is a safety feature. Saying the chair "looks different" is true but does not explain anything about safety.$q$, 'draft', '6593489f-ceb8-561a-8b3b-e3076c9e1598')
