  ('4a258ffe-a714-5de9-a35e-adfac63690e2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 2, Mr. Okonkwo says, "Practice makes perfect." Why does he use this adage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To remind her that all her practice has prepared her.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain that only perfect players can perform.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"To tell her she must practice more before going on.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To warn her that any mistake will ruin the show.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To remind her that all her practice has prepared her.$q$, $q$He follows the saying with "You have played this piece a hundred times," so he means her practice has made her ready. He is not asking her to practice more, since the show is about to begin.$q$, 'draft', '80aa67a6-66ba-5905-ac37-bf7cd62dc883')
