  ('d17dff06-9170-5897-ac5e-8ab399818fdf', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The word "bow" is a homograph. In paragraph 5, Priya "took a bow." What does "bow" mean in that sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a bend forward to thank the audience","is_correct":true},{"text":"a ribbon tied in two neat loops","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"a stick with strings used to play a cello","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"the front part of a large ship","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a bend forward to thank the audience$q$, $q$She "stood and took a bow" while the crowd clapped, so she bent forward to thank them. In paragraph 3 the other meaning appears, the stick she "drew across the strings," which is the tempting wrong answer.$q$, 'draft', '80aa67a6-66ba-5905-ac37-bf7cd62dc883')
