  ('63fc88a2-b260-5f0b-8d88-f28118a1c0f5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 2, Mr. Okonkwo says, "Your fingers know the way home." What does he mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her fingers will help her find the road back to her house later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She should stop playing and go home if she feels too scared.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She has forgotten the piece and must learn it again at home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Her fingers have practiced so much they will find the right notes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her fingers have practiced so much they will find the right notes.$q$, $q$Right before this, he says she has played the piece "a hundred times," so "home" stands for the familiar notes her fingers already know. He is encouraging her, not telling her to leave.$q$, 'draft', '80aa67a6-66ba-5905-ac37-bf7cd62dc883')
