values
  ('d1a06ab9-cde2-53dd-bd9e-9784d4534b51', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$In paragraph 1, the author writes, "An octopus is a living escape artist." What does this metaphor mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"An octopus performs magic tricks for people to watch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"An octopus is very good at getting out of tight spots.","is_correct":true},{"text":"An octopus is easy to catch and keep in one place.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"An octopus likes to paint pictures on the sea floor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-of-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An octopus is very good at getting out of tight spots.$q$, $q$The sentence before says its soft body "can squeeze through a gap as small as a coin," so the metaphor means it can escape almost anywhere. It is not a real performer.$q$, 'draft', 'be6f451d-b89d-521b-9668-dcbabc3d4534')
