  ('df69a8f3-5435-5a24-9033-fb8552c1cc99', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 3, the octopus "seems to vanish into thin air." What does this idiom mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It grows brighter so the shark notices it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It floats up out of the water into the sky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It swims far away to a different ocean.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It becomes impossible for the shark to see.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It becomes impossible for the shark to see.$q$, $q$The paragraph explains that the octopus changes color to "match the sea floor," so it blends in and seems to disappear. It does not actually leave the water or the area.$q$, 'draft', 'be6f451d-b89d-521b-9668-dcbabc3d4534')
