  ('9fdd3200-574d-5ef0-98c4-4b7f4198be97', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 2, Tomas "did not want to burn out too early." What does "burn out" mean here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"use up all his energy before the end","is_correct":true},{"text":"run too slowly to keep up with others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"step out of bounds and leave the course","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"get a sunburn from running outside","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$use up all his energy before the end$q$, $q$He follows the advice "Slow and steady wins the race" so he will still have energy later. The idiom is about running out of strength, not about heat or leaving the course.$q$, 'draft', 'cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a')
