   $q$In paragraph 3, the author writes, "his legs turned to lead." What does this metaphor mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His legs felt very heavy and hard to lift.","is_correct":true},{"text":"His legs were covered in gray mud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"His legs felt light and full of energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"His legs led him to the front of the race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His legs felt very heavy and hard to lift.$q$, $q$Lead is a heavy metal, and he is climbing "a giant wall of mud and roots," so his legs feel heavy. "Lead" here does not mean to go first, which is a different word spelled the same way.$q$, 'draft', 'cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a')
