   $q$In paragraph 2, the mail pouch "passed from hand to hand like a baton in a relay race." What does this simile show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"One rider carried the mail the whole way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The mail was handed from one rider to the next.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The mail was dropped often along the trail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The riders raced each other to win a prize.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The mail was handed from one rider to the next.$q$, $q$In a relay, each runner hands the baton to the next, just as "a new rider took over" after about seventy-five miles. The riders were a team, not racing against each other.$q$, 'draft', 'd596dcc2-6c8b-5890-bb6d-99d5a76dac15')
