   $q$In paragraph 5, Amara remembers that "every cloud has a silver lining." How does this proverb connect to her story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She would rather stay inside on cloudy days.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The weather turned sunny after a cloudy morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Moving was easy, so she never felt any sadness.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The hard move led to something good, a new friend.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The hard move led to something good, a new friend.$q$, $q$The proverb means something good can come from a bad time, and the last sentence says, "Moving had been hard, but it had led her to a new friend." The story never mentions the weather.$q$, 'draft', '40ee821a-033c-5050-8a63-60585f5cb2bf')
