   $q$In paragraph 6, Ms. Lindqvist says, "Two heads are better than one." Which event in the story best shows this proverb is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The coding club met in Room 12 every Thursday afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The frog hopped across the lily pads to reach a golden fly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Rafael groaned and said they had to start the game all over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"Hana found the wrong number, and Rafael fixed it so the game worked.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Hana found the wrong number, and Rafael fixed it so the game worked.$q$, $q$The proverb means two people working together can solve problems better than one, and Hana spotted the mistake while Rafael fixed it. Rafael groaning shows a problem, not teamwork solving it.$q$, 'draft', '52f07ced-071b-58b1-846c-9feb0fcfd543')
