   $q$The narrator says the glazed bowl was "the color of a rainy sidewalk." What does this description show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bowl was left outside in the rain overnight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The narrator is disappointed and thinks the bowl is ruined.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator is excited about how the bowl looks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Grandma Ines does not like the color of the glaze.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-character-views"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator is disappointed and thinks the bowl is ruined.$q$, $q$Right after this description the narrator says, "It looks terrible," so the gray comparison shows disappointment. The bowl was never outside; the rain is only a comparison.$q$, 'draft', '53b6544e-e45c-581f-a406-56a955919464')
