   $q$How is this poem organized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each stanza tells about one day from morning until night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"Each stanza describes a different animal that lives in the creek.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Each stanza tells about a different creek the speaker visits.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"Each stanza shows the same creek in a different season, in order.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each stanza shows the same creek in a different season, in order.$q$, $q$The stanzas begin "In spring," "In summer," "In fall" and "In winter," so they follow one creek through the year. Minnows appear in only one stanza, so the stanzas are not organized by animals.$q$, 'draft', 'f5e81445-8903-5af3-917d-8c1af0d5d08c')
