   $q$How does the last stanza connect back to the first stanza?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It introduces a new creek that the speaker likes better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It shows the creek drying up forever, the opposite of spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"It repeats the first stanza word for word to end the poem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The speaker looks forward to the loud spring creek, bringing the poem full circle.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker looks forward to the loud spring creek, bringing the poem full circle.$q$, $q$In the first stanza the creek likes to "shout," and in the last the speaker promises, "I'll hear you shout when cold days pass," which points back to spring. The creek is frozen, not dried up, and it is expected to return.$q$, 'draft', 'f5e81445-8903-5af3-917d-8c1af0d5d08c')
