   $q$What kind of narrator tells this fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The windmill, telling what it saw from the field","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-narrator-with-character"},{"text":"A narrator outside the story who is not a character","is_correct":true},{"text":"The farmer, describing the barn and the corn","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The weather vane, telling its own story with \"I\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-narrator-with-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A narrator outside the story who is not a character$q$, $q$The fable calls the characters "it" and "the farmer," so the narrator stands outside the story. The vane speaks with "me" only inside quotation marks, which is dialogue, not narration.$q$, 'draft', 'd5a9b747-cc36-555e-a2af-7a2d9f362593')
