-- Passage rg5-main-idea-summary-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5d645a1c-1943-5297-8275-79e3c6c3aa8e', 'rg5-main-idea-summary-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-main-idea-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Masters of Disguise$q$, $q$The octopus is one of the best hiders in the ocean. It has no shell and no bones, so it cannot protect itself with armor. Instead, it stays safe by staying out of sight.

An octopus can change its color in less than a second. Its skin holds thousands of tiny sacs filled with color. By squeezing or relaxing these sacs, the octopus can turn red, brown, white or speckled. It can match the sand, a rock or a patch of seaweed.

Color is not the only trick. An octopus can also change the texture of its skin. It can raise small bumps to look like rough coral or keep its skin flat to look like smooth stone. Some octopuses even fold their arms to look like floating plants.

When hiding does not work, an octopus has a backup plan. It can squirt a cloud of dark ink into the water. The ink hides the octopus for a moment while it jets away.

Because its body is so soft, an octopus can squeeze into tiny cracks. A large octopus can fit through a hole about the size of a coin. These skills together make the octopus very hard to catch.$q$, 'draft')
