   $q$What does the line "My hands forget what they knew" suggest about the speaker?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker's hands are too cold to move.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker is nervous and worried about playing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker never learned the song very well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker wants to play a different song.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker is nervous and worried about playing.$q$, $q$Together with "My mouth is dry as a paper sack," the line shows nerves before performing. The speaker plays the song "just right" at the end, so the speaker did know it.$q$, 'draft', 'ccc61179-fc80-5554-892f-a92044e0317a')
