   $q$According to the fable, why did the animals gather beneath the barn?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They were thirsty and wanted to ask where to find water.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They wanted to hide from the strong east wind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They were resting after their long walk south.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-event"},{"text":"They came to listen to the mole tell a story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They were thirsty and wanted to ask where to find water.$q$, $q$No rain fell, the pond "shrank to a muddy puddle," and the goat asks, "where can we find water?" The walk south happens after they gather, not before.$q$, 'draft', '57f3f8ef-e208-5c35-9fcb-3999632161c3')
