   $q$What can the reader infer about why the walk south did not help the animals?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The wind changed while they walked, so they lost their way home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The animals walked too slowly and turned back before reaching water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The weather vane only knew the wind's direction, not where water was.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The mole had already taken all the water from the southern pond.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The weather vane only knew the wind's direction, not where water was.$q$, $q$The rooster answers a question about water by saying "The wind is from the south," which is the only thing it knows. The animals find "only dry grass and dusty stones," and nothing says they gave up too early.$q$, 'draft', '57f3f8ef-e208-5c35-9fcb-3999632161c3')
