   $q$Which quotation best shows that the weather vane believes it knows more than it really does?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Above them, the rooster kept spinning.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"\"They gathered beneath the barn.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character"},{"text":"\"I see everything from up here. Ask me anything.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"The wind is from the east!\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"I see everything from up here. Ask me anything."$q$, $q$Claiming to "see everything" and inviting "Ask me anything" shows the rooster's pride, yet it cannot find water. Calling out the wind direction is something it really can do, so that line does not show it overestimating itself.$q$, 'draft', '57f3f8ef-e208-5c35-9fcb-3999632161c3')
