   $q$What does the sentence "This time, no one looked up" suggest about the animals?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They could not hear the rooster over the bubbling spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They were angry at the mole for not speaking up sooner.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character"},{"text":"They were too tired from walking to lift their heads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They no longer trusted the weather vane to guide them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They no longer trusted the weather vane to guide them.$q$, $q$Earlier the animals looked up to the rooster for answers, but its advice failed and the mole's worked, so ignoring it shows they stopped trusting it. The moral about "the loudest voice" supports this, while nothing suggests they could not hear.$q$, 'draft', '57f3f8ef-e208-5c35-9fcb-3999632161c3')
